@startuml revoke-and-unbind
!theme plain
title Broker v0, design only: ending access, grant revocation, task end, account withdrawal

actor "Owner / operator\nCLI as pinned OS principal" as P
participant "swarma-dispatcher\nown service OS account" as D
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot, no-argument sudo entry" as H
participant "swarma-credential-broker\nunprivileged broker service UID" as B

== a grant is revoked ==
P -> B: revocation.put (signed revocation envelope, §6.4)
B -> B: verify swarma-credential-broker revocation/1 signature\nunder the state lock: write the new revocation state\n(temp file, flush, rename, flush directory), update memory
B --> P: acknowledged (only after the state is durable)
B -> B: dispatcher revocation.check: revoked for affected chains;\nnext lease/renewal: lease_grant_revoked for the lease chain,\nlease_caller_revoked for the caller chain (method-specific refusals)

== the task ends ==
D -> B: unbind: binding_id; original unbind effect request_id
B -> B: durable receiver intent, then end leases and close UID connections;\npersist result and removal tombstone before acknowledgement (§7.2)
B --> D: recorded result and current removal state
opt reply lost or receiver recovery
  D -> B: effect.observe: original request_id, unbind, canonical-argument digest
  B -> B: authenticate original caller / operator; serialize with receiver journal
  B --> D: recorded (result + current state) | pending | rolled_back |\nnot_recorded | unavailable | contradictory
  D -> D: only authoritative evidence proves absence; unknown holds claim
end
D -> H: user.retire {generation: g-0193}\n(abbreviated helper request; distinct retire effect ID)
H -> H: state retiring: launcher refuses g-0193;\nstop processes, verify quiescence; (v1: egress stays denied)
H -> H: declared-key cleanup; delete home;\nremove account and group; state removed
note over D,H
  Ordinary retirement deletes the home; export only service-generated
  closed-schema metadata without agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies.
  Separate explicit operator home retention cannot guarantee confidentiality.
  Unbind tombstones remain for admissible retry/reconciliation (§7.2);
  expired/missing evidence is unavailable, never not_recorded.
end note
H --> D: removed
note over D,H: Future keeper integration (D-IDENTITY): after retirement,\ndispatcher separately revokes only identities registered as one-shot.\nStanding identities require a signed operator revocation;\nunbind/retire are not blanket identity revocation.
note over B: a recycled UID or a repeated label inherits nothing:\nbindings, grants and leases are keyed by generation

== the account is withdrawn ==
P -> B: account.revoke {account: owner/claude/personal}
B -> B: account state revoked; subsequent leases / renewals refuse lease_account_revoked (§8.2)
P -> P: revoke at vendor (Claude web interface, §10.1);\ntokens already copied end only there or at expiry
note over B
  Broker owns account/secret, grant/revocation, binding and lease files;
  helper owns ledger and retirement. Record writes atomic (§12.4).
  Material-deletion procedure / account.revoke commit point:
  unspecified in spec §5.3 / §13.2.
  [[../spec/broker.md#64-revocation Spec §6.4]]
  [[lease-recovery.puml M-CB2: crash after durable revoke and fail-closed repair]]
  [[record-states.puml M-CB3: independent record states and transition gaps]]
end note
@enduml
